## What this project is

{{ description or project_name }}. The agentic layer (stamped by
agentic-project-template) owns review loops, agent orchestration, LLM
dependencies, task and attribution conventions, and structure enforcement.
Language and build concerns live in the base project; do not confuse the two.

## Working rules

- Agent work is defined before it starts: a backlog task (`backlog-py task
  create`, ids `apt-…`) stating what done means — acceptance criteria or a
  definition of done. One task per unit of work.
- Agent work happens isolated: one worktree per task (`wt switch <branch
  named from the task id>`); never edit a shared checkout for task work.
  Start/finish procedure: `docs/task-workflow.md`.
- The fast loop never needs asking: every commit is queued for background
  review (roborev). Before claiming work done, check open findings for the
  branch (skill: `review-findings`) and fix what is real.
- The slow loop runs on demand (`mise run review-deep`) and when scheduled by
  the maintainer. Its report lands in `docs/reviews/`; its retro section may
  assign tasks — treat those as normal tasks.
- Repetitive AI usage is a candidate for deterministic tooling. When you
  notice a pattern repeating across sessions, record it in
  `docs/experiments.md` instead of doing it by hand a fourth time.
- Every skill you reference must be declared in `agents.toml` (dotagents).
  If an instruction names a skill that is not installed, that is a defect —
  report it, do not improvise the skill.
- Do not add secrets or machine-specific paths to committed configs.
  Personal tool configuration belongs to the user level, not this project.
- `.alint.yml` enforces repository shape; its `agent` output carries fix
  instructions — run what it says. `AGENTS.md` here is kept in step with the
  enforced rules; do not edit the managed section by hand.

## Commands

- `mise run install` — bootstrap tools and managed state (dotagents install)
- `mise run review-deep` — slow loop
- `mise run roborev-status` / `roborev-fix` — fast loop findings
- `mise run check` — alint + project checks

